<div class="w-full max-w-2xl rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-gray-900/60 p-6 md:p-8" data-test-lobby ...attributes>
  <div class="flex items-center mb-2">
    {{svg-jar "microphone" class="w-5 h-5 text-teal-400 mr-2"}}
    <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-teal-400">Voice interview · up to 8 minutes</span>
  </div>

  <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-50 mb-3">Can you explain what you built?</h1>

  <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
    Talk an AI interviewer through the code you wrote for
    <strong class="text-gray-100">{{@milestone.title}}</strong>
    in
    <strong class="text-gray-100">{{@repository.course.name}}</strong>. It asks 4 or 5 questions, you answer out loud, and your code stays on screen
    the whole time.
  </p>

  <ul class="space-y-3 mb-6 text-sm text-gray-300">
    <li class="flex items-start">
      {{svg-jar "code" class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-500 mr-3 shrink-0"}}
      <span>We'll ask how your code works, why you built it that way, and what would break it.</span>
    </li>
    <li class="flex items-start">
      {{svg-jar "chat-alt-2" class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-500 mr-3 shrink-0"}}
      <span>There are no trick questions. "I'm not sure" is a fine answer, and the interviewer won't correct you mid-call.</span>
    </li>
    <li class="flex items-start">
      {{svg-jar "check-circle" class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-500 mr-3 shrink-0"}}
      <span>At the end you get written feedback on each answer, pointing at the parts of your code it's about.</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="mb-6">
    <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 mb-2">Stages covered</div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5" data-test-stages-covered>
      {{#each @milestone.stages as |stage|}}
        <span class="rounded-sm bg-gray-800 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-gray-300" data-test-stage-covered>{{stage.name}}</span>
      {{/each}}
    </div>
  </div>

  <CourseInterviewPage::LobbyActions
    @isStarting={{@isStarting}}
    @onCaptionsToggle={{@onCaptionsToggle}}
    @onStartButtonClick={{@onStartButtonClick}}
    @shouldShowCaptions={{@shouldShowCaptions}}
    @startButtonLabel="Start interview"
  />

  <InterviewRecordingNotice class="mt-6">
    We record and transcribe the call so we can give you feedback. This is an experiment, so expect a few rough edges.
  </InterviewRecordingNotice>
</div>